    "title": "Abdominal pain requires ADR screening and reporting",
    "message": "Guidelines require all health workers to screen every patient encounter for suspected adverse drug reactions using the Drug Safety Screening checklist, and all suspected ADRs, whether mild or severe, must be recorded in ART cards, registers, and eMRS and reported. The patient reports abdominal pain with no fever and preserved appetite while on TDF/3TC/DTG since March 2023. The symptom checklist includes abdominal complaints among adverse events to be assessed at each visit. No cause has been documented, and no ADR screening or reporting action appears in today's plan.",
