    "alert_id": "P004_ABD_PAIN_EVAL_001",
    "title": "Abdominal pain on TDF warrants clinical evaluation",
    "message": "Guideline toxicity references list abdominal pain among adverse events associated with ART drugs, including upper abdominal pain with hepatotoxicity presentations. The patient has been on TDF/3TC/DTG for nearly three years and now reports abdominal pain without fever. TDF can cause renal tubular dysfunction and hepatotoxicity, though her creatinine of 82 umol/L 78 days ago is normal, which argues against significant TDF nephrotoxicity. Non-drug causes such as gastritis, infection, or other gastrointestinal pathology should also be considered. The clinician's plan documents the symptom but contains no evaluation, differential diagnosis, or monitoring orders.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Evaluate the abdominal pain clinically, consider TDF-related hepatotoxicity or renal effects, and investigate non-drug causes; repeat creatinine and liver function tests if indicated.",
